            {"id": "c", "text": "Rapid elasticity", "correct": True, "rationale": "Correct. Rapid elasticity is the ability to quickly scale resources outward (provision) and inward (de-provision) to match demand, often automatically. The scenario describes exactly this: auto-scaling in and out based on load."},
            {"id": "d", "text": "Shared resources", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. Shared resources (resource pooling) refers to the provider serving multiple tenants from the same physical infrastructure. While related to elasticity, it is not the characteristic being demonstrated by the auto-scaling behavior described."},
