            {"id": "b", "text": "Sandbox", "correct": True, "rationale": "Correct. A sandbox is an isolated VM environment used to run untrusted or potentially malicious code safely. Changes are contained within the sandbox; the production host is not at risk. Analysts commonly use sandboxes for malware analysis."},
            {"id": "c", "text": "Legacy software support", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. Legacy software support means running an outdated OS or application (e.g., Windows XP) in a VM for compatibility with old software. The scenario is about isolating malicious code, not running legacy software."},
